{"id": "1531036924922564858", "channel_id": "1531036924922564858", "author_id": "706262934485073951", "author_name": "bagels5899", "content": "I would like to preface this with the fact that I love the game, have been sticking with it for a solid time now and don’t plan on stopping anytime soon. Howhever, in recent times, Since about Vortice’s debut, a few problems I have been popping up that both upset and worry me as both a consumer and passionate fan of the game is the continued usage of Divine Realms, as well as an increased exalt cost with an Abolute Axiom that grants high amounts of aliemus.\n\nTo begin with divine realms, every unit since Vortice has had a divine version of their respective realm in their kit, these divine realms, while offering a different playstyle to the original do also offer a very non negligable boost to command cards, exalts, tentacle damage etc. I would like to know just how viable will be running teams without some access to a divine realm in the future, will the base realms be able to in any way for this increase besides the difference in approach? If possible, could the addition of divine realms not be as constant and instead be reserved to every so often to keep them unique? And this especially becomes more apparent in places like the Caro realm, where previous units where balanced in both their embryo generation and devour effects around 100/100 embryo bar, will new realms just make it more awkward for these pre divine realm units to function? and what about characters like Kathigu-Ra and mono chaos 24 who want/need to posse every turn despite Primordial Chaos seemingly wanting otherwise\n\n# CONTINUED ->", "timestamp": "2026-07-26T20:34:08.192000+00:00", "thread_id": "1531036924922564858", "edited_timestamp": "2026-07-26T21:00:57.479000+00:00", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 16}]}
{"id": "1531036948255346688", "channel_id": "1531036924922564858", "author_id": "706262934485073951", "author_name": "bagels5899", "content": "# ->\nSecondly, and the more worrying, since Saya characters have had extremely high Aliemus costs with a way of generating aliemus that can somewhat slow compared to their 100 aliemus counterparts… of which the problem arises where you notice that the character’s Absolute Axioms levy the aliemus constrains by giving them a decently potent source of Aliemus. When Absolute Axioms were introduced it was under the promise that it would only be a numerical boost and not be/fix a large part of a characters kit, then why is that slowly becoming the case now? If this will be the trend could you at least release more methods of obtaining aliemus be it new characters (who hopefully won’t have it tied behind a 200 aliemus exalt who gain better methods of regenrating aliemus through their Axiom) relics/wheels/etc. \n\nI do not bring these issues up from a place of malice but from a place of concern, will Morimens me moving into an era where you are expected to be using newer characters for their divine realms and characters with high aliemus costs that are levied with AA?\n\nplease consider what I have said and potentially give us a response reaffirming that these changes are done with good intentions\n\n# —- END OF POST —-", "timestamp": "2026-07-26T20:34:13.755000+00:00", "thread_id": "1531036924922564858", "edited_timestamp": "2026-07-26T21:01:25.907000+00:00", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Ramona_duel", "emoji_id": "1356053112292511815", "count": 2}, {"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 5}]}
